# Project Structure (FSD)

Follow **docs/project-structure.md** for all code in this repo. Summary:

## Layout under `src/`

- **features/** – Self-contained business features (components/, hooks/, *.store.ts, constants). One feature per folder (e.g. asset-editor, game-preview, game-settings, text-to-game, user-flow).
- **pages/** – Route-level components; compose features/widgets; minimal logic.
- **shared/** – Cross-feature only (api/, hooks/, lib/, ui/, queries/, utils/). API + DTOs in shared/api; server state in shared/queries; shared UI in shared/ui.
- **widgets/** – Reusable UI building blocks (e.g. Gizmo, Panel).
- **domain/** – Business rules and validators only (e.g. domain/game-setting/validators.ts).

## Dependency direction

```
pages → features → widgets → shared
  ↓
domain (no outward deps)
```

- Put new code in the correct layer; don’t let features depend on pages or domain depend on app layers.
- Server state: React Query in **shared/queries/**.
- Client/draft state: Zustand in feature-level **\*.store.ts**.

## Conventions

- Shared code used by 2+ features → **shared/**.
- Icons used in 2+ features → **shared/ui/icons/** (export via shared/ui).
- New feature: mirror existing feature folders (components/, hooks/, *.store.ts, constants).

Reference **docs/project-structure.md** for full structure, examples, and migration notes.
